        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "86af3f08-dcef-5ab7-8416-18b4571e6c08",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Middlewich\n- Events: Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival\n- Industries: salt production, chemical manufacture\n- Transport Systems: canal boats\n- Products: salt, coal, chlorine, soda ash, sodium carbonate\n- Concepts: industrial heritage\n\nFacts:\n- Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival builds on Middlewich's industrial heritage.\n- In Middlewich, canal boats were used to move coal and other raw materials for the production of salt.\n- In Middlewich, canal boats were also used to move salt out of town for direct use or for use as a raw material in manufacturing chemicals such as chlorine and soda ash.\n- Sodium carbonate is also known as washing soda, soda ash, and soda crystals.\n- In its monohydrate form, sodium carbonate is also known as crystal carbonate.\n- Sodium carbonate is the water-soluble sodium salt of carbonic acid.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bdb21e81-b8b5-5d4c-8aad-19c150fc8551",
        "text": "Page: Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival. Sentence: The festival builds on the town's industrial heritage in which canal boats were used to move coal and other raw materials in the town for the production of salt, and then move the salt out of town, either for use directly, or as a raw material in the manufacture of chemicals such as chlorine and soda ash.\nPage: Sodium carbonate. Sentence: Sodium carbonate (also known as washing soda, soda ash and soda crystals, and in the monohydrate form as crystal carbonate), NaCO, is the water-soluble sodium salt of carbonic acid.",
